{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>A young man, a Hebrew, a slave.</b> Cursed are the wicked — their kindness is not whole; they mention him in language of disgrace." "<b>A young man.</b> A fool, and not fit for greatness." "<b>A Hebrew.</b> He does not even recognize our language." "<b>A slave.</b> And it is written in the laws of Egypt that a slave does not rule, nor does he wear the garments of nobles." "<b>Each man according to his dream.</b> According to the dream, and close to its subject."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:54.058482283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}